WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.439 --> 00:00:04.445
Unit fifteen. Understanding File Types!

2
00:00:05.384 --> 00:00:10.202
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:10.252 --> 00:00:13.847
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.897 --> 00:00:18.209
Today we learn about Understanding File Types. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.076 --> 00:00:23.267
File type. Say it with me. File type!

6
00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:31.117
Extension. Say it with me. Extension!

7
00:00:34.595 --> 00:00:38.662
Document. Say it with me. Document!

8
00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:46.563
Image file. Say it with me. Image file!

9
00:00:50.053 --> 00:00:54.553
Video file. Say it with me. Video file!

10
00:00:58.069 --> 00:01:02.269
.jpg. Say it with me. .jpg!

11
00:01:05.744 --> 00:01:10.573
.pdf. Say it with me. .pdf!

12
00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:17.716
Format. Say it with me. Format!

13
00:01:21.264 --> 00:01:34.741
A file type, shown by its extension like .jpg or .pdf, tells the computer what format it is. A document, image file... / video file each has a different type.

14
00:01:34.791 --> 00:01:39.080
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:40.082 --> 00:01:45.554
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:46.754
Document!

17
00:01:47.893 --> 00:01:53.186
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:53.236 --> 00:01:54.511
.pdf!

19
00:01:55.693 --> 00:02:05.987
Did you know? The letters after the dot in a filename, called the extension (like .jpg or .docx), tell your computer how to open that file!

20
00:02:06.037 --> 00:02:08.386
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:09.404 --> 00:02:19.110
Think and answer. What file type do you think a photo is usually saved as?

22
00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.374
Great answer!

23
00:02:21.312 --> 00:02:27.211
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:27.261 --> 00:02:30.270
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

